Okay, so I investigated this and there's unfortunately nothing we can do on our end.

## Why it doesn't work

We use the `_input` for our inputs - that's how we can support things like `z.string().transform(v => ...)` - and we can't change that. In zod, a branded string still has the _input_ of just an unbranded `string`:

### Code
```ts
import { z } from 'zod';

const brandedString = z.string().brand("branded");

type Input = typeof brandedString["_input"];
//    ^? type Input = string
type Output = typeof brandedString["_output"];
//    ^? type Output = string & z.BRAND<'branded'>
```

### Playground

https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgLzgXzgMyhEcDkyEAJvgNwBQFAxhAHYDO8ARlAIZ3ECmxAyjFGB0A5nAC8KAHRNBIgBQBKSaw7E5AIhWce6hZQowAnmC5wAknTABXeBKMmImOFu58BQ4QG11AfSHWYdQBdSgB6ULhIuAA9AH4DY1MAeRsA8Th7Lkdndm03WS9fCFSbYLCIqLiqIA


## Thoughts

I am unsure how came the gang over at zod came to the decision there to make the input and output different here but they likely did it for good reasons. Changing it would likely be seen as a breaking change within zod even if not many people likely leverage the `_input` of zod schemas.


